villain BaronBlade
name Baron Blade
challenge Decoy Impulsion Beam
When Baron Blade flips to his second side, the villain trash is not placed on top of the villain deck and the villain deck is not shuffled.
At the start of the villain turn, if there are 15 or more cards in the villain trash, Baron Blade's Terralunar Impulsion Beam activates, pulling the moon into the earth. Game Over.

variant MadBomberBaronBlade
name Mad Bomber Baron Blade
base BaronBlade
unlock Defeat standard Baron Blade. Then, while fighting Citizen Dawn, destroy Citizens Blood, Sweat, and Tears in the same round.
requires BaronBlade CitizenDawn?
challenge Nanobot Power Armor
Reduce damage dealt to Baron Blade by 2.

villain CitizenDawn
name Citizen Dawn
challenge Solar Retribution
Whenever a Citizen card is destroyed, Citizen Dawn deals the hero target with the highest HP 3 fire damage.

villain GrandWarlordVoss
name Grand Warlord Voss
challenge Hostile Take Over
Whenever Grand Warlord Voss flips, play the top card of the Villain deck.

villain Omnitron
name Omnitron
challenge Redundant Systems
For every 7 damage Omnitron is dealt in a round, the heroes may choose one villain component to be destroyed. Ignore the second line of text on villain component cards.

variant OmnitronII
name Omnitron II
base Omnitron
unlock Defeat standard Omnitron. Then, while fighting Grand Warlord Voss, destroy two spaceships in the same round.
requires Omnitron GrandWarlordVoss?
challenge Cosmic Overdrive
The value of (H) is doubled in this game.

villain Ambuscade
name Ambuscade
from Ambuscade
challenge Trap Master
At the start of the game, all trap cards in Ambuscade's deck are turned face up.
Whenever a trap card would be discarded, first the top card of the villain deck is played, then the trap card is discarded.
Whenever the villain trash is shuffled into the villain deck, all trap cards are turned face up.

villain TheChairman
name The Chairman
from RookCity
challenge Chemical Immortality
At the start of the villain turn, The Chairman regains (H) HP.
At the start of the villain turn, The Operative regains (H) HP.

villain TheMatriarch
name The Matriarch
from RookCity
challenge Carrion Wasteland
Domain cards are indestructible.

villain PlagueRat
name Plague Rat
from RookCity
challenge Noxious Stench
At the start of the villain turn, Plague Rat deals each non-villain target 1 toxic damage.

villain Spite
name Spite
from RookCity
challenge Strung-Out Maniac
Spite can regain HP past his maximum HP.

variant SpiteAgentOfGloom
name Spite: Agent of Gloom
from RookCity
base Spite
unlock Defeat standard Spite. Then, defeat GloomWeaver by having 3_villain relics in the villain trash. At least two of the following must be in play: Cursed Acolyte, Profane Zealot, Chosen Disciple, or Ophidia the Deceiver. No Voodoo Pin may be in play.
requires Spite Gloomweaver
challengereq SpiteAgentOfGloom SkinwalkerGloomweaver
challenge Summoner and Overlord
After Spite is defeated, he is immediately replaced by Skinwalker Gloomweaver without altering the environment or any of the heroes or hero cards. Heroes do not regain HP or draw cards. The game resumes at the start of Gloomweaver's turn.

villain AkashBhuta
name Akash'Bhuta
from InfernalRelics
challenge Eco-Titan
Akash'Bhuta is immune to environment damage and villain damage.

villain Apostate
name Apostate
from InfernalRelics
challenge Demon Lord
Whenever a demon card enters play, the top card of the villain deck is played.

villain TheEnnead
name The Ennead
from InfernalRelics
challenge Eternal Spellcraft
Every villain one-shot has all three symbols as keywords.

villain Gloomweaver
name GloomWeaver
from InfernalRelics
challenge Chaos Dimension
Villain relics are indestructible.

variant SkinwalkerGloomweaver
name Skinwalker GloomWeaver
from InfernalRelics
base Gloomweaver
unlock Defeat standard Spite and GloomWeaver. Then, do one of the following:\\1)_Defeat Spite: Agent of Gloom in Rook City on his "Broken Vessel" side with zero cards under the Safe House and at least five Victims in play. \OR\2)_Be defeated by Spite: Agent of Gloom in Rook City on his "Agent_of_Gloom" side with no more than two Drug cardsface up. Spite must have destroyed at least five Victims.
requires Spite Gloomweaver SpiteAgentOfGloom
challengereq SpiteAgentOfGloom SkinwalkerGloomweaver
challenge Summoner and Overlord
The game begins against Spite: Agent of Gloom. After Spite is defeated, he is immediately replaced by Skinwalker Gloomweaver without altering the environment or any of the heroes or hero cards. Heroes do not regain HP or draw cards. The game resumes at the start of Gloomweaver's turn.

villain MissInformation
name Miss Information
from MissInformation
challenge Sloppy Saboteur
Whenever a clue card enters play, the top card of the villain deck is played.

villain LaCapitan
name La Capitan
from ShatteredTimelines
challenge Timeless Crew
At the start of the game, cards are revealed from the top of the villain deck until (H) crew cards are revealed and put into play. Other revealed cards are shuffled back into the villain deck.
Whenever La Capitan flips, the crew card with the highest HP in the villain trash is moved into play.

villain TheDreamer
name The Dreamer
from ShatteredTimelines
challenge Frail Child
Increase damage dealt to The Dreamer by 5.

villain IronLegacy
name Iron Legacy
from ShatteredTimelines
challenge Final Justice
At the start of the villain turn, the villain trash is shuffled and cards are revealed until an ongoing card is revealed and put into play. Other revealed cards are returned to the villain trash.

villain Kismet
name Kismet
from ShatteredTimelines
challenge Burning Talisman
At the start of each hero's turn, if The Talisman is in their play area, it deals that hero character card (H) fire damage.

variant TricksterKismet
name Trickster Kismet
from ShatteredTimelines
base Kismet
unlock Lose a game against regular Kismet in The Block, with at least K.N.Y.F.E., The Argent Adept, and Fanatic on the team. Over the course of the game, the Talisman must spend more full turns in hero play areas than full turns in the villain play area.
requires Kismet TheBlock Knyfe? ArgentAdept? Fanatic?
challenge Patient Punisher
Whenever a jinx card enters a hero play area, Kismet deals each target in that play area 2 energy damage.
Whenever Kismet reduces any target to 0 or fewer HP, play the top card of Kismet's deck.

villain Deadline
name Deadline
from WrathOfTheCosmos
challenge Endling Workmanship
Villain device cards are indestructible.

villain Infinitor
name Infinitor
from WrathOfTheCosmos
challenge Pervasive Horrors
Reduce damage dealt to manifestation cards by 2.

variant HeroicInfinitor
name Heroic Infinitor
from WrathOfTheCosmos
base Infinitor
unlock Defeat Infinitor with damage dealt by a Construct. Captain Cosmic must be the first hero and no heroes may be incapacitated. Each different Manifestation must enter play at least once.
requires Infinitor CaptainCosmic?
challenge Drawn to the Edge
At the start of the villain turn, the top card of Infinitor's deck is revealed. If it is a manifestation, it is put into play. If not, it is shuffled back into Infiltrator's deck and each manifestation in play is restored to its maximum HP.

villain KaargraWarfang
name Kaargra Warfang
from WrathOfTheCosmos
challenge Illustrious Bloodsword
Whenever a gladiator card enters play, the top card of the title deck is revealed and put under that gladiator card with the effects still visible.

villain Progeny
name Progeny
from WrathOfTheCosmos
challenge Ultimate Scion
Scion cards do not destroy other scion cards upon entering play until there are 5 of more scion cards in play.

villain WagerMaster
name Wager Master
from WagerMaster
challenge All Fun and Pain
Whenever a villain card is flippedf face-down, each hero target deals itself 1 psychic damage.

villain Chokepoint
name Chokepoint
from Chokepoint
challenge Steel-Singer
Whenever a non-villain card is destroyed, it is put face-down in the villain play are (unless it is already face-down in the villain play area).
Whenever a card is put face-down in the villain play area, Chokepoint regains 2 HP and deals each hero target 2 energy damage.

teamvillain TeamBaronBlade
name Baron Blade (Team)
from Vengeance
challenge Mastermind
Baron Blade is immune to villain damage.

teamvillain TeamErmine
name Ermine
from Vengeance
challenge Canny Thief
At the start of the game, Subtle Diversion and Uncatchable are put into play.

teamvillain TeamFriction
name Friction
from Vengeance
challenge Sturdy Tech
The Shock Dampeners card is indestructible.

teamvillain TeamFrightTrain
name Fright Train
from Vengeance
challenge All Aboard
As long as Fright Train is a target, redirect all hero damage to Fright Train.

teamvillain TeamProletariat
name Proletariat
from Vengeance
challenge The Will of the People
Targets named Proletariat are immune to psychic damage.

teamvillain TeamAmbuscade
name Ambuscade (Team)
from VillainsOfTheMultiverse
challenge Slaughterhouse Six's True Leader
During setup, before revealing cards from the top of Ambuscade's deck, search the deck for Glamour and put her into play.
As long as there are any other villain targets in this play area, Glamour is indestructible and immune to damage, even if Ambuscade is incapacitated.

teamvillain TeamBiomancer
name Biomancer
from VillainsOfTheMultiverse
challenge All According to Plan
Whenever a fleshchild is destroyed, Biomancer regains (H) HP. Then, if Biomancer is at his max HP, play the top card of Biomancer's deck.

teamvillain TeamBugbear
name Bugbear
from VillainsOfTheMultiverse
challenge Mystic Hunt
At the start of the game, note the hero character with the lowest HP. That hero and Bugbear are nenemes this game.
Whenever bugbear deals damage to a hero target that is not his nenemis, he also deals an equivalent amount of damage to any of his nemeses in the game.
If Bugbear ever reduces his nemesis to 0 or fewer HP, restore Bugbear to his max HP.

teamvillain TeamLaCapitan
name La Capitan (Team)
from VillainsOfTheMultiverse
challenge Pursued Through Time
Whenever La Capitan plays a one-shot, La Capitan deals each target 2 psychic damage.
Whenever one of La Capitan's ongoing cards is destroyed, reveal the top card of La Capitan's deck. If it is not an ongoing card, put it into play. Otherwise, discard it.

teamvillain TeamCitizensHammerAndAnvil
name Citizens Hammer and Anvil
from VillainsOfTheMultiverse
challenge Dawn's Chosen
Whenever a hero uses a power, discard the top card of that hero's deck. If the discarded card was an ongoing card, Citizen Hammer deals that hero 2 fire damage. Otherwise, Citizen Hammer & Citizen Anvil each regain 2 HP.

teamvillain TeamGreazer
name Greazer
from VillainsOfTheMultiverse
challenge Heels on Fire
Impeccable Pompadour is no longer indestructible. At the end of Greazer's turn, if the Impeccable Pompadour is not in play, shuffle Greazer's trash into his deck, then play the top card of Greazer's deck.
Increase damage dealt by Greazer to each hero target in the play area with the Living Paycheck by 1.

teamvillain TeamMissInformation
name Miss Information (Team)
from VillainsOfTheMultiverse
challenge Masked Intentions
The first time a player discards a card each turn, each villain target regains 1 HP.
At the end of Miss Information's turn, play the top card of the villain deck belonging to the villain character card in play with the highest HP.

teamvillain TeamTheOperative
name The Operative
from VillainsOfTheMultiverse
challenge Breath of the Dragon
The Operative's max HP for this game is 20.
At the start of The Operative's turn, The Operative deals each hero target 3 fire damage.

teamvillain TeamPlagueRat
name Plague Rat (Team)
from VillainsOfTheMultiverse
challenge Delicious Handlers
Whenever Plague Rat deals damage to a handler, he regains that much HP.
Whenever a handler is destroyed, reveal the top card of Plague Rat's deck. If it is not a handler or Revocorp Backup, put it into play. Otherwise, discard it and Plague Rat deals (H) melee damage to the target other than himself with the lowest HP.

teamvillain TeamSergeantSteel
name Sergeant Steel
from VillainsOfTheMultiverse
challenge Combat Maneuvers
Whenever an agent enters play, reduce damage dealt to that agent by 2 until the start of Sergeant Steel's next turn.
Whenever an agent's F.I.L.T.E.R. icon is activated, that agent regains 2 HP.

